{"description":"A local Unix domain socket exposing an event stream and a small command surface, so a running client can be driven and observed from the shell.\n\nThis is deliberately delivered in the MVP even though slash commands, webhooks and plugins are all deferred to phase 4: it is the substrate all of them would need, and on its own it already makes walkie scriptable. Building it first is what allows the plugin runtime to be postponed honestly rather than merely dropped.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. The socket is created with owner-only permissions and removed cleanly on exit, including after an unclean shutdown of a previous run.\n2. Sending a message and reading the event stream both work from a shell script with no walkie-specific tooling.\n3. Events are line-delimited and parseable by standard command-line tools.\n4. The socket is local only; it is not reachable over the network in any form.\n5. A client with no reader attached to the event stream does not block or leak."}